==== Stock firmware web interface ====
The stock firmware web interface does not seem to accept the OpenWrt images.


==== TFTP ====
OpenWrt images can be flashed from within the U-boot bootloader via TFTP.

**<color #ed1c24>Some devices may have a restricted boot loader that pretends to try TFTP recovery but does not request anything.</color>**

In these cases, you may want to flash a working boot loader for that device. A good summary on this topic can be found [[https://mcmillan.website/rewriting-mt7628an-bootloader/|here]]. The unlocked bootloader can be found [[https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B-rjYLkZBDZrVnloaDdFWFA1RDQ]|here]].

  - Set your computer to 192.168.10.100
  - Set up a TFTP server on your computer
  - Rename the OpenWrt ''xxxx-sysupgrade.bin'' image as ''firmware.bin'' and place it in the root folder of the TFTP server
  - Power off the device and connect an Ethernet cable from its LAN port to your computer
  - Press the WPS button (and keep it pressed)
  - Power on the device
  - After a few seconds, when the LAN LED stops blinking very fast, release the WPS button
  - After one minute or so, OpenWrt will be running and accessible as with any other device, normally at ''192.168.1.1''. If nothing happens, retry with the WAN/LAN port.


